                            <comment id="492766" author="JIRAUSER19234" created="Thu, 9 Apr 2026 19:46:12 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Opened &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20110" title="Fix slow recovery-small test_136 " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20110"&gt;LU-20110&lt;/a&gt; to track / fix this issue.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="492034" author="JIRAUSER19234" created="Mon, 30 Mar 2026 21:34:53 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Reopened to address recovery-small test_136 taking much longer (1000s+ ) after this patch was landed.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="491797" author="JIRAUSER19234" created="Tue, 24 Mar 2026 22:44:45 +0000">&lt;p&gt;I think I see the issue. The debug info was useful here.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class="alternate" type="square"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;20:18:51 — node onyx-157vm144 is confirmed powered off (100% ping loss)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;20:34:47 — "rebooted" message prints (~16 minutes later)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is one of the only test to use FAILURE_MODE=HARD. The log printing tries to get the uptime info from the powered off node and hangs when it can't make the connection, until it finally times out and continues along. This should be easy enough to fix by adding earlier forced timeout to the uptime_info call.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="491794" author="JIRAUSER19234" created="Tue, 24 Mar 2026 22:10:33 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Taking a look at this. Seems rather odd? You wouldn't think adding a few extra logs and increasing wait time from 1 -&amp;gt; 5 seconds would lead to an increase by hundreds of seconds for that test.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="491760" author="adilger" created="Mon, 23 Mar 2026 23:31:04 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Still seeing recovery-small test_136 being much slower (+1000s for this one subtest) than before this debug patch was landed.  It would be good to understand if this patch is providing useful information, or if the performance impact could be reduced some way:&lt;br/&gt;
 &lt;span class="image-wrap" style=""&gt;&lt;a id="63703_thumb" href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/attachment/63703/63703_recovery-small-test_136-1.png" title="recovery-small-test_136-1.png" file-preview-type="image" file-preview-id="63703" file-preview-title="recovery-small-test_136-1.png"&gt;&lt;img src="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/thumbnail/63703/_thumb_63703.png" style="border: 0px solid black" role="presentation"/&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="489426" author="adilger" created="Fri, 27 Feb 2026 22:36:45 +0000">&lt;p&gt;It looks like this patch has significantly increased the duration of recovery-small test_136:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/reports?test_set_script_id=f36cabd0-32c3-11e0-a61c-52540025f9ae&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=d0b69ab2-c341-11e8-a2b9-52540065bddc&amp;amp;source=duration_trend#redirect" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/reports?test_set_script_id=f36cabd0-32c3-11e0-a61c-52540025f9ae&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=d0b69ab2-c341-11e8-a2b9-52540065bddc&amp;amp;source=duration_trend#redirect&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
 &lt;span class="image-wrap" style=""&gt;&lt;a id="63214_thumb" href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/attachment/63214/63214_recovery-small-test_136.png" title="recovery-small-test_136.png" file-preview-type="image" file-preview-id="63214" file-preview-title="recovery-small-test_136.png"&gt;&lt;img src="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/thumbnail/63214/_thumb_63214.png" style="border: 0px solid black" role="presentation"/&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It started to show slow test runs before the patch landed (up to 1000s vs. 90s without patch) on 2026-01-07, and then got consistently slow after 2026-02-04 when the patch landed:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?client_branch=master&amp;amp;server_branch=master&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=f36cabd0-32c3-11e0-a61c-52540025f9ae&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=d0b69ab2-c341-11e8-a2b9-52540065bddc&amp;amp;start_date=2026-01-07&amp;amp;end_date=2026-01-07&amp;amp;source=sub_tests#redirect" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?client_branch=master&amp;amp;server_branch=master&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=f36cabd0-32c3-11e0-a61c-52540025f9ae&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=d0b69ab2-c341-11e8-a2b9-52540065bddc&amp;amp;start_date=2026-01-07&amp;amp;end_date=2026-01-07&amp;amp;source=sub_tests#redirect&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It isn't clear looking at the test logs why it is so much slower, but possibly the test is now actually doing what it was &lt;em&gt;supposed&lt;/em&gt; to be doing?  ... or not, but it deserves some investigation.  If the test duration cannot be reduced, then this subtest should be added to the &lt;tt&gt;SLOW&lt;/tt&gt; list.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="486914" author="pjo" created="Sat, 7 Feb 2026 19:17:20 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Merged for 2.18&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
